#* {{RQ:Thackeray Henry Esmond|volume=II|chapter=I Go on the Vigo Bay Expedition, Taste Salt Water and Smell Powder|page=96|passage=He '''rid''' to the end of the village, where he alighted and ſent a man thence to Mr. Tuſher with a meſſage that a gentleman of London would ſpeak to him on urgent buſineſs.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Mrs. Rinehart|journal=Time|date=28 Apr 1923
|passage=It is characteristic of her that she hates trains, that she arrives from a rail-road journey a nervous wreck; but that she can '''ride''' a horse steadily for weeks through the most dangerous western passes.}}
